# {{studlyName}} Icons for Laravel

[![Latest Version on Packagist](https://img.shields.io/packagist/v/{{packageName}}.svg?style=flat-square)](https://packagist.org/packages/{{packageName}})
[![Total Downloads](https://img.shields.io/packagist/dt/{{packageName}}.svg?style=flat-square)](https://packagist.org/packages/{{packageName}})
[![License](https://img.shields.io/packagist/l/{{packageName}}.svg?style=flat-square)](LICENSE.md)

Beautiful {{studlyName}} icons for Laravel applications via the [Ichava](https://github.com/ichava/ichava) icon ecosystem.

## Requirements

- PHP 8.3 or higher
- Laravel 10, 12, or 13+
- [ichava/ichava](https://github.com/ichava/ichava) ^1.0

## Installation

Install the package via Composer:

```bash
composer require {{packageName}}
```

The package will auto-register its service provider.

### Publish Configuration (Optional)

```bash
php artisan vendor:publish --tag={{kebabName}}-icons-config
```

### Seed Icons to Database (Optional)

If you want to use the icon browser or search functionality:

```bash
php artisan ichava:database seed --package={{packageName}}
```

## Usage

### Package-Specific Blade Component

The simplest way to use icons in your Blade templates:

```blade
{{-- Basic usage --}}
<x-{{kebabName}}-icons-icon name="home" />

{{-- With Tailwind classes --}}
<x-{{kebabName}}-icons-icon name="user" class="w-6 h-6 text-blue-500" />

{{-- With custom attributes --}}
<x-{{kebabName}}-icons-icon name="settings" class="w-8 h-8" id="settings-icon" data-tooltip="Settings" />

{{-- Icon in a category/variant folder --}}
<x-{{kebabName}}-icons-icon name="category/icon-name" />
```

### Generic Ichava Blade Component

Use the generic Ichava component with the full icon path:

```blade
{{-- Using slash notation --}}
<x-simtabi-ichava::icon name="{{packageName}}::home" class="w-6 h-6" />

{{-- Using dot notation --}}
<x-simtabi-ichava::icon name="{{packageName}}::category.icon-name" class="w-6 h-6" />
```

### Ichava Helper Function

Use the global `ichava()` helper for more flexibility:

```blade
{{-- Basic usage --}}
{!! ichava('{{packageName}}::home') !!}

{{-- With attributes array --}}
{!! ichava('{{packageName}}::user', ['class' => 'w-6 h-6 text-blue-500']) !!}

{{-- Using dot notation for path --}}
{!! ichava('{{packageName}}::folder.subfolder.icon-name') !!}
```

### Fluent API

For programmatic icon rendering with method chaining:

```php
use function Simtabi\Laranail\Ichava\ichava;

// Basic fluent usage
ichava('{{packageName}}::home')
    ->class('w-6 h-6 text-blue-500')
    ->render();

// With multiple attributes
ichava('{{packageName}}::user')
    ->class('w-8 h-8')
    ->id('user-icon')
    ->attr('data-tooltip', 'User Profile')
    ->render();

// Get SVG content without rendering
$svgContent = ichava('{{packageName}}::home')->toSvg();
```

### In Controllers/Services

```php
use Simtabi\Laranail\Ichava\Facades\Ichava;

class MyController extends Controller
{
    public function index()
    {
        // Get icon as SVG string
        $icon = Ichava::render('{{packageName}}::home', [
            'class' => 'w-6 h-6',
        ]);

        // Check if icon exists
        $exists = Ichava::exists('{{packageName}}::home');

        return view('welcome', compact('icon'));
    }
}
```

## Icon Path Format

Icons follow the Ichava path convention:

```
vendor/package::category/icon-name
vendor/package::category.icon-name
```

**Examples:**

```blade
{{-- Root level icon --}}
{!! ichava('{{packageName}}::home') !!}

{{-- Icon in subfolder (using slash) --}}
{!! ichava('{{packageName}}::social/facebook') !!}

{{-- Icon in subfolder (using dot notation) --}}
{!! ichava('{{packageName}}::social.twitter') !!}
```

## Configuration

The package configuration is located at `config/{{kebabName}}-icons.php`:

```php
return [
    // Enable/disable the icon set
    'enabled' => env('{{snakeNameUpper}}_ICONS_ENABLED', true),

    // Custom path to icons (optional)
    'path' => env('{{snakeNameUpper}}_ICONS_PATH', ...),

    // Enable icon caching for better performance
    'cache' => [
        'enabled' => true,
        'prefix' => '{{prefix}}',
    ],
];
```

### Environment Variables

```env
# Enable/disable the icon set
{{snakeNameUpper}}_ICONS_ENABLED=true

# Custom path to icons (optional)
{{snakeNameUpper}}_ICONS_PATH=/path/to/icons
```

## Available Icons

Browse all available icons using the Ichava browser:

```bash
# Start the icon browser
php artisan serve
# Visit: http://localhost:8000/ichava/browser
```

Or list icons via command line:

```bash
php artisan ichava:info icons --package={{packageName}}
```

## Auto-Update Command

Update icons from the latest source:

```bash
php artisan ichava:update-{{kebabName}}-icons

# With custom source
php artisan ichava:update-{{kebabName}}-icons --source=/path/to/icons

# Force update without confirmation
php artisan ichava:update-{{kebabName}}-icons --force
```

## Adding Your Own Icons

1. Place your SVG files in `resources/assets/svg/files/`
2. For multi-variant icons, organize by variant: `files/regular/`, `files/solid/`, etc.
3. Update `resources/assets/svg/config.json` with metadata
4. Clear cache: `php artisan ichava:cache clear`

### Icon Guidelines

- Use valid SVG format
- Remove unnecessary attributes (width, height are added dynamically)
- Use `currentColor` for fill/stroke to enable color customization
- Keep file names lowercase with hyphens (e.g., `arrow-left.svg`)

